dungeons.dimension.description.spider_cave=A mysterious cave overrun with Spiders and their eggs, tread lightly and bring lots of torches.
dungeons.dimension.description.ancient_crypt=A long forgotten chamber that houses many undead, all of whom's tale has been lost to time.
dungeons.dimension.description.mushroom_dimension=A mysterious field of Mushrooms and.. well, not much else. Be careful of the Cows, they have gone mad.
dungeons.dimension.description.deepsea_monument=A mysterious monument found deeper than any known ocean can go. It begs the question of.. what even built this place>
dungeons.dimension.description.cursed_halls=A labyrinth like series of halls that make up the cellar of some large castle somewhere far, far away.
dungeons.dimension.description.ominous_castle=A large, brutalist castle that is trapped in eternal thunder.
dungeons.dimension.description.desert_tomb=An underground sanctuary that houses many lost spirits, it is likely that this tomb has connections to the Nameless One.
dungeons.dimension.description.woodland_mansion=While it may seem ordinary on the surface, the layout of this Mansion is utterly illogical and unnatural from the perspective of any builder.
dungeons.dimension.description.frosted_fjord=A chilling wasteland covered in ice and snow, it seems a large series of ruins and camps can be found here, too.
dungeons.dimension.description.soul_ruins=Nobody really knows how there could be so many souls here, but some things we are better off not knowing.
dungeons.dimension.description.slimy_sewer=A mysterious underground network of tunnels and pipes, overran by slime and seeming to not.. actually connect to anything..?
dungeons.dimension.description.creepy_stronghold=A dark, mysterious structure, now overrun by an infestation. It seems whoever built it used to worship some forgotten, broken God.
dungeons.dimension.description.obsidian_fortress=An Illager-Fortress full of dark energy. High above the clouds, Hot lava is cooled into the Obsidian used to create their strongest Monstrosity.
dungeons.dimension.description.woodland_prison=Below every Mansion is its prison, a place harboring alot of ominous energy and spirits reaching out to the beyond.
dungeons.dimension.description.outer_end=No matter how far you travel, you may never see plantlife like this anywhere else.. If you can even call what you find here "plants".
dungeons.dimension.description.pumpkin_forest=A cozy forest in the middle of nowhere that is unfortunately riddled with undead.. be careful in case the Pumpkins come alive, too.
dungeons.dimension.description.silent_woods=Not a single pleasant creature could be found here before the monsters arrived, which is why this place earned the name Silent Woods.
dungeons.dimension.description.faraway_fortress=A Fortress hidden away in the far corners of the Nether, harboring monsters and lots and lots of lava.
dungeons.dimension.description.corrupted_jungle=A misty jungle with a permenant haze in the air, but be careful, because some of the plants you find here are truly frightening!
dungeons.dimension.description.lower_forge=Even deeper below the Fiery Forge, it is possible that this is the true forge of the Redstone Monstrosity.. and god knows what else.
dungeons.dimension.description.grand_bastion=A tricky maze that has seemingly fallen apart, in spite of this, it still remains a grand structure that is teeming with gold. Perhaps the Piglin Merchant was once a resident?
dungeons.dimension.description.coral_cave=Coral Cavel lies beneath a deep underwater trench, with this seemingly reflecting on the creatures living in it, as well as the sediment itself.
dungeons.dimension.description.forgotten_citadel=A lost city on the edge of the void, what remains of its large complexes now overran by dangerous end mobs.
dungeons.dimension.description.misty_peak=These peaks are ripe with precious emeralds, which might explain why there are so many Illagers, too.

